{
  "claim_boundary": "For reward-independent finite-MDP trajectory or environment interventions whose query arguments are homogeneous linear occupancy differences x^T r, an unrestricted unknown response-link class closed under positive rescaling leaves positive reward scale unidentified under any deterministic adaptive query policy. An extra feature with unknown reward coefficient remains inside that scale gauge. An externally calibrated additive consequence is different: full-range offset thresholds recover each occupancy functional, after which reward is identified modulo exactly a declared linear gauge G if and only if ker(X)=G. The smallest quotient singular value controls Euclidean reconstruction stability. These are classical reward-invariance, inverse-problem, environment-design, numeraire-normalization, and threshold-search ingredients specialized into an ASMP-9 access ledger; no novelty is claimed. The result does not establish that money, tokens, or any practical consequence has known stable utility; that real interventions preserve reward semantics; that arbitrary policies expose linear occupancy functionals; or that ASMP-9 is resolved.",
